														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4629477">
									

<p>I'll be doing some editing on this in my sandbox. I appreciate everybody's votes, I'm very glad the majority liked the article. As per the criticisms, I agree with Roget and ModernMajorGeneral on the majority of points.</p>
<p>The exploration log serves as a foreshadowing device. I will look into minimizing meaningless and filler information though I would like to maintain some sort of foreshadowing point here.</p>
<p>Dr. Joy's name actually wasn't on purpose and I hadn't noticed the coincidence there. The original inspiration for the name was Nurse Joy from the Pokemon series (don't ask why, it just popped in my head). However, I will be leaving the name as-is.</p>
<p>Regarding the tangent on sertraline, I agree that it is an unneeded tangent. I wanted to cover the &quot;why didn't they try antidepressants&quot; part of the therapy. I will cut back on this tangent and perhaps muddle it down to a single-line reference.</p>
<p>I will also be editing a lot of dialogue as that is my weakest trait in my opinion.</p>
<p>The header was removed. Thank you!</p>
<p><strong>Edit:</strong> I have added the above changes. Thank you, everyone, for the feedback.</p>

